1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,999
"Love is measured in dollars, dear."

2
00:00:02,999 --> 00:00:06,826
My future mother-in-law slid a list across the table.

3
00:00:06,826 --> 00:00:10,582
Bride's family contribution: fifty thousand dollars.

4
00:00:10,582 --> 00:00:14,698
And my father, a small-town carpenter, was left standing.

5
00:00:14,698 --> 00:00:16,647
Nobody offered him a chair.

6
00:00:17,547 --> 00:00:22,143
Dad had spent three months of evenings carving walnut spoons with our names on them.

7
00:00:22,143 --> 00:00:24,715
She picked one up with two fingers and laughed.

8
00:00:24,715 --> 00:00:25,535
"Wooden spoons?

9
00:00:25,535 --> 00:00:29,365
If you can't manage this much, maybe this marriage isn't a good idea."

10
00:00:29,365 --> 00:00:34,344
The spoon hit the floor, and my father got down on his knee in his only suit to pick it up.

11
00:00:35,244 --> 00:00:37,263
My fiancé stared at his water glass.

12
00:00:37,263 --> 00:00:41,301
Then she made Dad pay half of a nine hundred dollar dinner he never ate.

13
00:00:41,301 --> 00:00:44,890
On the drive home he whispered, "I'm sorry your dad isn't more."

14
00:00:44,890 --> 00:00:48,591
That night, he sanded those spoons again until two in the morning.

15
00:00:49,491 --> 00:00:50,505
Here's the thing.

16
00:00:50,505 --> 00:00:53,130
I was living that night for the second time.

17
00:00:53,130 --> 00:01:02,019
In my first life, she secretly used my bakery as collateral for a two hundred thousand dollar loan, and my father collapsed when the collectors came.

18
00:01:02,019 --> 00:01:03,808
Then I woke up a year earlier.

19
00:01:03,808 --> 00:01:05,240
This time, I hit record.

20
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:07,508
She mocked his workshop.

21
00:01:07,508 --> 00:01:09,674
She cut his name from the invitations.

22
00:01:09,674 --> 00:01:15,145
And one rainy afternoon, I found Dad outside a pawn shop, holding my late mother's wedding ring.

23
00:01:15,145 --> 00:01:17,311
"It's all I have to give you, Gracie."

24
00:01:17,311 --> 00:01:19,932
I held him on the sidewalk and made a promise.

25
00:01:20,832 --> 00:01:28,201
Then a man in a leather jacket and a gold watch walked into my bakery and looked around like he was pricing everything.

26
00:01:28,201 --> 00:01:30,307
"Families help each other, friend.

27
00:01:30,307 --> 00:01:32,784
When they don't, life gets complicated."

28
00:01:32,784 --> 00:01:35,880
My phone, in my apron pocket, recorded every word.

29
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:42,195
Two weeks before the wedding, she pushed a mortgage on my building across the table.

30
00:01:42,195 --> 00:01:43,548
"Do not tell Richard.

31
00:01:43,548 --> 00:01:45,418
Sign, or forget the wedding."

32
00:01:45,418 --> 00:01:49,350
That night she texted me: "Who does a carpenter think he is?"

33
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:52,831
So I called the one man who had been quietly watching.

34
00:01:52,831 --> 00:01:53,927
My father-in-law.

35
00:01:54,827 --> 00:01:57,774
At the family dinner, she spread the list out again.

36
00:01:57,774 --> 00:01:59,134
Again, no chair for Dad.

37
00:01:59,134 --> 00:02:04,290
Then Richard walked out of his study, carried a chair over himself, and sat my father down.

38
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,537
"Put that away, Diane.

39
00:02:05,537 --> 00:02:07,974
Before you embarrass yourself any further."

40
00:02:08,874 --> 00:02:12,328
The lawyer laid out the loan, the mortgage, the recordings.

41
00:02:12,328 --> 00:02:15,197
The so-called broker was arrested at the airport.

42
00:02:15,197 --> 00:02:18,008
Her lake house and jewelry went to pay her debt.

43
00:02:18,008 --> 00:02:20,936
And Richard said, "My father was a carpenter too."

44
00:02:20,936 --> 00:02:23,922
She got down on her knees and apologized to my dad.

45
00:02:24,822 --> 00:02:28,800
On my wedding day, Dad walked me down the aisle in that same suit.

46
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:33,681
The favors were two hundred walnut spoons he carved, and Richard paid full price.

47
00:02:33,681 --> 00:02:35,610
Love is not measured in dollars.

48
00:02:35,610 --> 00:02:37,719
Hear the whole story on Life Story.
